<v Ike Sriskandarajah>According to a statement from the Standing Committee, they were worried about what precedent it would set, what conflicts of interests hanging his painting could cause. And Pablo hadn't gotten permission from the event organizers to put his painting into their event.
<v Ike Sriskandarajah>根据常设委员会的一份声明，他们担心这会开创什么样的先例，挂上他的画会引起什么样的利益冲突。而且巴勃罗在把画放入活动现场前，并没有获得活动组织者的许可。

00:15:16.930 --> 00:15:51.180
<v Ike Sriskandarajah>Icarus, son of Daedalus, soaring over the Isle, was enthralled by his own new ability. He couldn't help wanting to go higher. Pablo, son of Luis, didn't want to only stay in the back of the press conference with the other scribes. Couldn't this event to honor Frederick Douglass also honor Pablo, too? Maybe if he'd asked permission, gone through channels, this all might have worked out differently. I floated that idea by Pablo.
<v Ike Sriskandarajah>伊卡洛斯，代达罗斯之子，翱翔在岛屿上空，被自己新获得的能力所吸引。他忍不住想要飞得更高。路易斯之子巴勃罗，不想仅仅和其他写稿人一起待在新闻发布会的后面。这个纪念弗雷德里克·道格拉斯的活动难道不能也纪念一下巴勃罗吗？也许如果他请求许可，走正规程序，这一切可能会有不同的结果。我把这个想法提给了巴勃罗。

