<v Ike Sriskandarajah>Ego-- it's what makes you pick up a box of stolen art supplies and think, without any experience, I will be a transformational force in the US Capitol. But it's also ego that propels you to the front of a press conference, with your painting under your arm, and sends you crashing back to Earth. The Potomac is lousy with wax and feathers.
<v Ike Sriskandarajah>自我——这让你拿起一盒被盗的艺术用品，心想：没有任何经验，我将成为美国国会大厦的一股变革力量。但同样是自我，推动你带着画走到了新闻发布会的最前沿，然后让你狠狠地摔回地面。波托马克河到处都是蜡和羽毛。

00:17:00.830 --> 00:17:24.470
<v Ike Sriskandarajah>A couple hours after we talk, Pablo sends me a note. He's back in the Capitol. He says, for the first time, he feels small in this place that once made him feel big. The next day, he sends me another note. He sounds like himself again. He figured it out. He's launching his campaign to run for Standing Committee.
<v Ike Sriskandarajah>我们在谈话几小时后，巴勃罗给我发了一条信息。他回到了国会大厦。他说，这是他第一次在这个曾经让他感到伟大的地方感到渺小。第二天，他又给我发了一条信息。他又变回了那个他自己。他想通了。他要发起竞选活动，去争取常设委员会的席位。

00:17:24.470 --> 00:17:57.000
<v Pablo Manriquez>But luckily, I'm not eligible to run for the Standing Committee for at least another year, if not two. So I decided that, while I can't be on the ballot until probably 2028, I am going to start campaigning on Monday. So I registered the domain dailypressgallery.com, and I started writing an agenda. Part of my agenda is, of course, to repeal the prohibition that they put on journalist art in the Capitol.
<v Pablo Manriquez>但幸运的是，我至少还要再等一年，如果不是两年，才有资格竞选常设委员会。所以我决定，虽然我可能要到2028年才能出现在选票上，但我周一就要开始竞选活动了。所以我注册了域名dailypressgallery.com，并开始撰写一份议程。我的议程的一部分，当然是废除他们对记者在国会大厦创作艺术品的禁令。

